    A-3.21 fixup3: T12.6 in-place shrink (valid, 8192→4096)
    
    Fixes Steward's finding: T12.6 simulated an invalid in-place GROW
    (4096→8192) where the original block only had 4096 bytes capacity.
    
    FIX: Rewrote T12.6 as a valid in-place SHRINK:
      1. Allocate fresh 8192-byte block (real capacity = 8192)
      2. Track it (size=8192, in tracked range)
      3. Enable g_t12_force_inplace
      4. Shrink to 4096 via normal_realloc_tracked()
      5. Verify: same pointer returned, tracked size=4096, data preserved
      6. The shrink is VALID because 8192 >= 4096 (block has capacity)
    
    Both sizes (8192 and 4096) are >= MIN_TRACK_SIZE, so track_free
    and track_alloc are both exercised — the same-address path in
    normal_realloc_tracked() is genuinely tested.
    
    normal_realloc_tracked() (production shared function) is UNCHANGED.
    
    Results: 133 tests (+4 from expanded T12.6), exit 0.
    TSan: exit 0, 0 data races.

